hi this is presh talwalkar in this video  i'm going to explain the math behind why  you could multiply two numbers between  11 and 19 in your head  in the previous video we said if you  wanted to do 13 times 12 you could do a  series of steps where you added and  multiply different  portions of the numbers together to get  to the answer of 156  so we're going to go through the algebra  and see why this is actually a  legitimate method  a number between 11 and 19 can be  written as 10 plus x  where x is a number between 1 and 9.  so if we're multiplying two of these  numbers together  we have 10 plus x times 10 plus y  the first step of the process  was to take the entire number 10 plus x  and add it to the digit y  so we have  10 plus x plus y  to that result  we added a digit 0 which is the same as  multiplying by 10.  the second step of the process was to  take the units digits of both numbers x  and y  and multiply them together  so that would give us x y  the final step was to add these together  so doing some algebra  the first step would give us 100 plus 10  times the quantity x plus y  and the second step in green  gives us x times y  so this is the algebraic result of our  process  and if you check the math this is  exactly what you get by expanding the  two terms 10 plus x times 10 plus y  so in fact our three-step process  will give us the correct answer  i hope you liked this video please  subscribe to my channel  you can also catch me on my blog  mindyourdecisions or on twitter at  preshtalwalker
 

